IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-rules`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) -- the questions of the ATTORNEY: here typically a family member appointed under an
-- injured person's enduring power of attorney, who may run or settle the claim, receive the damages or compensation
-- and manage them.
--
-- SEAT: a second seat (CLAUDE.md, ruled 2026-10-21), for the party the Act puts duties and liabilities on. "Am I
-- eligible?", "May I act now?", "May I buy property in both our names?", "May I make this gift, and must I record it?",
-- "Must I keep my money separate?", "May I be paid?", "May I resign?", "Whom must I tell?", "Could I be made to pay
-- compensation, or be relieved?". It draws on the same rules as poa-seat.l4, so the two seats cannot disagree about the
-- law; the mirror cases in poa-cases-attorney.l4 ask the same facts from both seats. The answers are the rules' own
-- choices, worded from the principal's side ("my attorney"); the attorney reads them as about themself.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts and calls the rules of poa-rules.l4. No question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Powers of
-- Attorney Act 2014, Version No. 007 (26 April 2021), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Powers of Attorney Act 2014: the questions of the attorney`

§§ `Becoming the attorney`

@export Am I eligible to be appointed attorney under this enduring power of attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 3, 22(4), 28)? You must be 18 or over, not an insolvent under administration, and not the principal's paid care worker, health provider or accommodation provider; for financial matters, a dishonesty conviction must have been disclosed to the principal and recorded in the power. Being on a government carer payment for caring for the principal does not make you a care worker.
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `matters` IS A `Matters the attorney is for` @desc What you would be attorney for: for personal matters only; for financial matters only (including the principal's injury claim); or for both personal and financial matters
      `insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an insolvent under administration (an undischarged bankrupt, or under a personal insolvency agreement or arrangement not yet complete)
      `dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of an offence involving dishonesty punishable by at least 3 months' imprisonment, anywhere
      `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you told the principal and it is recorded in the power (answer no otherwise)
      `paid to care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid, from any source (including the principal's compensation), for services caring for the principal
      `carer payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a carer payment or other government benefit for providing home care for the principal
      `health provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide health care to the principal in the practice of a profession or in the course of business
      `accommodation provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, professionally or administratively, responsible for or involved in providing the principal's accommodation
GIVETH A `Whether this person is eligible to be my attorney`
`Am I eligible to be the attorney` MEANS
    `s 28 -- whether this person is eligible to be my attorney` `an individual` `matters` `my age` `insolvent` `dishonesty` `disclosed` (`s 3 -- this person is my care worker` `paid to care` `carer payment` `health provider`) `health provider` `accommodation provider` FALSE

@export May I act as attorney for the principal now on this matter, such as running or settling their injury claim (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 3, 22(2), 39, 41, 83)? From the making of the power unless it names a later time; whatever it says, while the principal lacks capacity for the matter; and once you began because they lacked capacity, even after they regain it. If VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order, only so far as VCAT authorises. Assumes the power is in force and you have accepted it.
GIVEN `scope` IS A `What my power covers` @desc What the power covers: personal matters only; financial matters only; both; specified matters including this one; or specified matters not including it
      `matter` IS A `Kind of matter` @desc The matter: a financial matter (money, property, or a legal matter about them, such as the injury claim); a personal matter; or medical treatment
      `start` IS A `When I said my power begins` @desc When the power says it begins: nothing specified; immediately; when the principal ceases to have decision making capacity for the matter; or another time, circumstance or occasion
      `time come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it names another time, circumstance or occasion: whether it has come (answer no otherwise)
      `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal now lacks decision making capacity for this matter
      `began acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already begun acting on this matter because the principal lacked capacity
      `administration order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has made an administration order for the principal
      `guardianship order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has made a guardianship order for the principal
      `VCAT authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is such an order: whether VCAT has authorised you to act despite it (answer no otherwise)
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may act now`
`May I act as attorney now` MEANS
    `ss 22, 39, 41, 83 -- whether my attorney may act now` `scope` `matter` `start` `time come` `lacks capacity` `began acting` `administration order` `guardianship order` `VCAT authorised`

@export Must I notify anyone before I first act because the principal has lost capacity (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 40)? Yes: before you first act on a matter because the principal lacks capacity for it, take reasonable steps (such as posting to their last known address) to notify each person the power says should be told. Not doing so does not invalidate what you do.
GIVEN `first time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are about to act on this matter for the first time because the principal lacks decision making capacity for it
      `names people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power names people who should be notified
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I notify anyone before I first act` MEANS
    `s 40 -- I must notify before acting` `first time` `names people`

§§ `My duties in dealing with the principal's money and affairs`

@export May I enter into a transaction in which my interests (or my relative's, business associate's or close friend's) may conflict with my duty to the principal, such as buying property in both our names with their damages (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 63, 64, 65)? Not unless the principal authorised it beforehand, VCAT authorised it, or it is validated (by the principal while capable, or by VCAT once completed). You must act honestly, diligently, in good faith and with reasonable skill and care, and avoid conflicts unless authorised (s 63).
GIVEN `financial attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an attorney for financial matters
      `conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is or may be a conflict between your duty to the principal and your interests or those of your relative, business associate or close friend
      `exception` IS A `Exception the transaction falls under` @desc Whether it is: no exception; a gift made under s 67; maintenance of the principal's dependant under s 68; dealing with property you and the principal hold jointly (or a loan or guarantee for it); or acquiring property to be held jointly with the principal (or a loan or guarantee for it)
      `capacity then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal had decision making capacity for the matter when the transaction was entered into
      `principal authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal authorised, before it, this transaction, this kind, or conflict transactions generally
      `VCAT authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT authorised it, or the kind, or conflict transactions generally, before it
      `completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transaction has been completed
      `principal validated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal validated it afterwards at a time they had decision making capacity for it
      `VCAT validated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT validated the completed transaction
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may enter into the transaction`
`May I enter into this transaction` MEANS
    `ss 64, 65 -- whether my attorney may enter into the transaction` `financial attorney` `conflict` `exception` `capacity then` `principal authorised` `VCAT authorised` `completed` `principal validated` `VCAT validated`

@export May I make a gift of the principal's property or money (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 67(1), (2))? Only as an attorney for financial matters, only if the power does not forbid it, the gift is reasonable given the principal's finances, and it is a seasonal or special-event gift to the principal's relative or close friend, or a donation of a kind the principal made or might be expected to make. It may go to you or your family.
GIVEN `financial attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an attorney for financial matters
      `forbidden` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a condition or restriction in the power forbids or limits this gift
      `reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift is reasonable given all the circumstances, in particular the principal's financial circumstances
      `seasonal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to the principal's relative or close friend and of a seasonal nature or for a special event (such as a birth or marriage)
      `donation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a type of donation the principal made while capable, or might reasonably be expected to make
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I make this gift` MEANS
    `s 67(1) -- my attorney may make the gift` `financial attorney` `forbidden` `reasonable` `seasonal` `donation`

@export Must I keep a written record of this gift, setting out its amount and recipient (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 67(3), (4))? Yes if it goes to you, your relative or close friend, or an organisation you are connected with, and its total value is at least the prescribed amount (or $100 if none is prescribed). Every gift is still a financial dealing you must record in the accounts (s 66).
GIVEN `connected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift is to you, your relative or close friend, or an organisation with which you have a connection
      `value` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value of the gift in dollars
      `prescribed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount prescribed by the regulations for s 67(3), in dollars (0 if none is prescribed; the regulations are not deposited)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I keep a written record of this gift` MEANS
    `s 67(3) -- I must keep a written record of the gift` `connected` `value` `prescribed`

@export Must I keep accurate records and accounts of this dealing (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 66)? Of every dealing and transaction for financial matters, and of every material one for personal matters. VCAT may order them lodged and audited (s 116(1)(e), (f)).
GIVEN `financial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dealing or transaction is for a financial matter
      `material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a personal matter: whether the dealing is material (answer yes or no; it does not matter for a financial one)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I keep records of this dealing` MEANS
    `s 66 -- I must keep records of the dealing` `financial` `material`

@export May I pay for the needs of the principal's dependant out of the principal's property (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 68)? Only as an attorney for financial matters, only if the power provides for it, and no more than is reasonable given the principal's finances unless the power allows more.
GIVEN `financial attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an attorney for financial matters
      `power provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power provides for maintaining the principal's dependants
      `reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount is no more than is reasonable given all the circumstances, in particular the principal's finances
      `power allows more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power allows more than a reasonable amount
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I provide for the principal's dependant` MEANS
    `s 68 -- the attorney may provide for the dependant` `financial attorney` `power provides` `reasonable` `power allows more`

@export Must I keep my own property separate from the principal's (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 69)? Yes, as an attorney for financial matters, except property you and the principal own jointly, or acquire jointly in place of jointly owned property. Pay the principal's damages or compensation into their own account, not yours.
GIVEN `financial attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an attorney for financial matters
      `joint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property is owned jointly by you and the principal, or acquired jointly in place of jointly owned property
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I keep my property separate` MEANS
    `s 69 -- the attorney must keep the property separate` `financial attorney` `joint`

@export Am I entitled to be paid for acting as attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 63(1)(c), 70)? Not unless the power specifically authorises it or the law does; you must not use the position for profit.
GIVEN `power authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power specifically authorises paying you
      `law authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether some law authorises it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to be paid` MEANS
    `s 70 -- the attorney is entitled to be paid` `power authorises` `law authorises`

@export What happens if I, as one attorney, disagree with the principal's other attorney about a matter (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 71, 72)? The personal matters attorney's decision prevails and the financial matters attorney must implement it, unless (for several attorneys) the power or VCAT says otherwise; if implementing it would seriously deplete the principal's finances, the financial attorney must apply to VCAT instead.
GIVEN `several` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you act severally and each of you has authority for the matter
      `otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power, or a VCAT order, says how such a disagreement is resolved
      `depletion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether implementing the personal matters decision would seriously deplete the principal's financial resources
GIVETH A `What happens when my attorneys disagree`
`What happens if I disagree with the other attorney` MEANS
    `ss 71, 72 -- what happens when my attorneys disagree` `several` `otherwise` `depletion`

§§ `Ending my role (only if I want to stop, or something has happened to me)`

@export May I resign as attorney now (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 56-61)? At any time while the principal has capacity for the matter; when they do not, if another attorney has power for the matter or an able and willing alternative attorney does, otherwise only with leave of VCAT or the Supreme Court. An alternative attorney not yet acting may resign; one who is acting needs leave. Use the prescribed form and tell the others.
GIVEN `alternative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an alternative attorney
      `acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an alternative attorney: whether you are acting in the attorney's place (answer no otherwise)
      `principal capable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal has decision making capacity for the matter
      `another attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another attorney has power for the matter
      `alternative willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing to act
GIVETH A `Whether the attorney may resign now`
`May I resign now` MEANS
    `ss 56, 59 -- whether the attorney may resign now` `alternative` `acting` `principal capable` `another attorney` `alternative willing`

@export Whom must I notify, in the prescribed form, that my appointment has been revoked because I became insolvent, the principal's paid carer, health or accommodation provider, or (for financial matters) was convicted of dishonesty (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 54(3)-(6))? The principal if they have capacity for the matter, and every other attorney and alternative attorney; if the principal lacks capacity and there is no other attorney or alternative, their nearest relative, or the Public Advocate if you cannot reach the nearest relative. An empty answer means no notice is required.
GIVEN `revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your appointment has been revoked by s 54(1) (you became an insolvent under administration, the principal's paid care worker, health provider or accommodation provider, or as a financial attorney were convicted or found guilty of a dishonesty offence, after appointment)
      `principal capable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal has decision making capacity for the matter you had power for
      `another attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is another attorney under the power
      `alternative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is an alternative attorney under the power
      `can reach relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to notify the principal's nearest relative
GIVETH A LIST OF `Who must be told`
`Whom must I notify that my appointment ended` MEANS
    `s 54(3), (4) -- who must be told` `revoked` `principal capable` `another attorney` `alternative` `can reach relative`

§§ `My liability (only if something has gone wrong)`

@export Could I be ordered to compensate the principal for a loss I caused (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 73-77)? The Supreme Court or VCAT may order it for a loss caused by your contravening the Act while acting as attorney, even if you were convicted, the power was invalid or revoked, or the principal has died (then to the estate). Not where you acted on the Court's or VCAT's advice or order without misleading it, or relied in good faith on a power you did not know was invalid or revoked, and not for any part you are relieved of.
GIVEN `contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss was caused by your contravening the Act's enduring power provisions while acting as attorney
      `court advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted in compliance with advice, a direction or an order of the Supreme Court or VCAT, without knowingly giving it false or misleading information
      `invalid or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power was invalid or had been revoked when you acted
      `good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you acted in good faith without knowing, or having reason to believe, that it was invalid or revoked (answer no otherwise)
      `relief` IS A `Relief from liability` @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved you of your personal liability: no relief; relieved of part; or relieved of all
      `principal died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal has died
GIVETH A `Whether I can be compensated`
`Could I be ordered to compensate the principal` MEANS
    `ss 73-77 -- whether I can be compensated` `contravention` `court advice` `invalid or revoked` `good faith` `relief` `principal died`

@export Could the Supreme Court or VCAT relieve me of personal liability for a contravention (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 74)? Yes, of all or part, if it considers that you acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused.
GIVEN `liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are or may be personally liable for a contravention of the Act's enduring power provisions
      `honest and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT considers you acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Could I be relieved of personal liability` MEANS
    `s 74 -- the court may relieve me` `liable` `honest and reasonable`

@export What is the maximum penalty if I dishonestly use the enduring power of attorney to gain money for myself or another, or to cause the principal loss (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 135(3), (4))? 5 years' imprisonment or 600 penalty units or both; a company, 2400 penalty units; even if the power was invalid or revoked. The answer is in penalty units; 0 years means no imprisonment.
GIVEN `company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate (a trustee company)
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`What is the maximum penalty if I use the power dishonestly` MEANS
    `s 135 -- the maximum penalty` `company`
